# See https://help.github.com/articles/ignoring-files/ for more about ignoring files.

# dependencies
node_modules
.pnp
.pnp.*
.yarn/*
!.yarn/patches
!.yarn/plugins
!.yarn/releases
!.yarn/versions

# testing
coverage

# next.js
.next/
out/

# production
build
dist

# turbo
.turbo

# briefing-worker local harness output: briefs it generated and the traces of
# the runs that made them. Real model output against real search results, so it
# is per-machine and disposable — see apps/briefing-worker/README.md §Watching.
.briefings/

# briefing-worker local harness output: cover letters drafted by `letter`. A
# letter is written in a candidate's voice from their own CV, so it is the last
# thing that should land in a shared repository.
.letters/

# misc
.DS_Store
*.pem

# claude code (personal, per-machine overrides)
.claude/settings.local.json

# debug
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*

# env files (can opt-in for committing if needed)
.env*

# lambda deploy artifact (built from dist/ on demand)
lambda.zip
# ...except the tiny fixture the terraform tests plan against. filebase64sha256
# reads the zip at plan time, so the suite needs *a* file there and must not
# need a build first.
!infra/aws/tests/fixtures/lambda.zip

# terraform: provider binaries and modules, per-machine
.terraform/
# state and plans. state holds every attribute terraform has read, plans hold
# resolved variable values — neither belongs in a diff. `.terraform.lock.hcl`
# is deliberately NOT ignored: pinning provider hashes is the point of it.
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
*.tfplan
tfplan
crash.log
crash.*.log
# variable files: the same resolved-values argument as plans
*.tfvars
*.tfvars.json
# ...except the root's own, which is configuration rather than resolved values:
# a bucket name, a function name and the alerting address, none of them secret
# and all of them already in the READMEs. Committed so that `terraform apply`
# needs no flags and a half-configured apply is not expressible. If this
# repository ever becomes public, drop alert_email from it and pass
# TF_VAR_alert_email instead — it is a flat variable so that override works.
!infra/aws/terraform.tfvars
# per-machine backend bucket, see infra/aws/bootstrap/README.md
backend.hcl
# per-machine cli config and local overrides
override.tf
override.tf.json
*_override.tf
*_override.tf.json
.terraformrc
terraform.rc

# vercel
.vercel

# neon (linked project/branch ids, written by `neon link` / `neon checkout`)
.neon

# typescript
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts

# Prisma Client is generated on build (`pnpm --filter @workspace/db generate`)
packages/db/src/generated/

# claude code worktrees (scratch checkouts, never part of the repo)
.claude/worktrees/
